# P1a-CTL (CONTROL, PRODUCTION BYTES): the prefix exactness-shared arm on the production audited profile, on the production base image. Production's prefix reuse has NEVER had an exactness verdict on cards
# (cancelled at 84 min once, at go-live once). The gate's own box for this plan is 10,800 s. NEVER CANCEL IT: the docker timeout ends it.
# VERDICT: PASS = the arm verdict PASS and every ship P1 read (eight agents, every pair identical, a packed round with 2+ live users, hits byte-equal to their solo cold twins, window digests equal, no program compiled by a hit after its cold twin);
# FAIL = any FAIL; otherwise NO-VERDICT(reason: TIMEBOX, INFRA, NOT_EXERCISED, RERUN) with the turns completed and the last row recorded. A FAIL is a PRODUCTION FINDING: the driver raises an ALERT line and the owner decides after the window
# whether prefix-reuse.off is needed (the window itself goes on: production is already down). Only INFRA or RERUN is re-run once under a reserve tag; a TIMEBOX NO-VERDICT is not retried with the same box.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the BASELINE window (README.md and ORDER.txt hold the window; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/baseline-window and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN (ORDER.txt has each job's tag). Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The window runs ONLY on today's production ENGINE: every job serves the production base image tp4-serve-10 (the engine bytes are production's; production's thin layer on top of it is NOT exercised) and the production profile family
# c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix (the -audit twin where a gate needs the extent audit: the same engine and env plus audit flags). No window image is built. No job here moves :latest or places a model.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset prefix
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-10
C2_PREFIX_PLAN=exactness-shared
C2_PREFIX_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-audit
C2_PREFIX_BASELINE=none
